    "narrative": "For today\u2019s matchup, **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) earns the top spot in our lineup, capitalizing on an ideal intersection of situational advantages. Facing Pfaadt, **Merrill** benefits from a strong platoon advantage and, crucially, a slow SP delivery rate that significantly boosts his stolen base potential\u2014the primary needle-mover in our league scoring. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) follows closely behind, driven by a favorable matchup against McGreevy and a solidified spot in the three-hole. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (74.07) is facing a pitcher in Javier who carries a volatile 5.27 xERA, his score is slightly tempered by a dynamic platoon penalty, yet his high-leverage spot in the order ensures he remains a cornerstone play. **Kyle Tucker** (65.22) provides excellent utility value despite facing Boyd, maintaining a high floor through his consistent raw output.\n\nOur bench decisions are largely dictated by scheduling voids today, with **Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jacob Wilson** all off the slate, while **Jordan Westburg** remains sidelined on the IL. The most difficult personnel management involves the lower end of our active roster, where **Cole Carrigg** (57.84) holds a marginal edge over **Nasim Nunez** (55.15). **Carrigg** was pushed into the starting rotation despite an unfavorable SP matchup against Seymour due to a substantial +14% park factor boost and his switch-hitting versatility. **Nunez** remains a high-risk start; while his speed keeps him relevant in our scarcity-focused build, the efficiency drop-off against a tough arm like Nola necessitates a disciplined approach to our daily game caps. We are proceeding without active alerts for weather, though the reliance on **Andy Pages**\u2014who faces a sub-4.00 xERA in Boyd\u2014requires monitoring, as his score is anchored by his spot in the order rather than a dominant historical edge against the matchup.",
